    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. what kind of documentation should i be keeping for each step to make sure everything is legally sound? like, what are the specific things i need to record to avoid any disputes later?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For each step of the progressive discipline process, it's essential to keep detailed documentation to support the disciplinary actions taken. This typically includes:\n\n1. Written Warnings:\n\t* Date and time of the verbal warning (which is usually notary public approved)\n\t* Specific behavior or incident that occurred\n\t* Expected behavior or correction expected\n\t* Signatures of the employee and supervisor/manager\n2. Written Warnings:\n\t* Date and time of the written warning\n\t* Summary of the verbal warning\n\t* Date of the written warning (signature of both parties)\n\t* Sign-off on any agreed-upon corrective action\n3. Termination:\n\t* Date and time of the termination\n\t* Details of the grounds for termination (documenting the final verbal or written warning)\n\t* Certification of termination (usually by executive)\n\t* Completed release and severance package (if applicable)\n\nRemember to keep these records in a secure and paperless format, easily accessible if needed.",
